subgraph HEAD["▶ &nbsp; START HERE &nbsp; ▶ &nbsp; THE QUESTION"]
    direction TB
    Q["<b>To what extent do AgentFormer attention weights give faithful<br/>explanations of the interactions that influence pedestrian<br/>trajectory predictions?</b><br/>Read attention as a graph. Mask edges. Predict again. Measure the shift."]
    SCOPE["ETH / UCY · 5 scenes · 2.5 Hz · public weights · inference only<br/>66,676 rows · 1,950 pedestrians · <b>univ holds 60 percent of the rows</b><br/>the frozen design: stride 5 · 481 windows · effective n = 156 by time block<br/><b>FAITHFULNESS, NOT CAUSALITY.</b> This is evidence about the MODEL.<br/>It is not evidence about how people walk. Say association, never cause.<br/>out of scope: perception · edge deployment · orchestration"]
    WHY["<b>WHY THIS DATA AND THIS MODEL</b><br/>ETH / UCY is the benchmark AgentFormer released its 5 checkpoints on.<br/>It is public, anonymised, and already in world coordinates,<br/>so no perception step and no camera model enter the study.<br/>AgentFormer makes the interaction graph EXPLICIT, so one edge can be masked.<br/>The weights are public, so we train nothing. 8 in / 12 out is the benchmark protocol."]
end

