subgraph HY["src/hypotheses/ · one file, one claim · ★ PREM · EVERY FILE EXISTS"]
    direction TB
    Y0["<b>design.py</b> · BUILT AND FROZEN · one-sided · alpha = 0.05<br/>stride 5 · 481 windows · design effect 3.08 · effective n 156<br/>minimum effect 0.592 · power 0.80 · PRIMARY n_removed = 1.<br/>the sweep is secondary. the rest is exploratory.<br/>the design effect comes from eda/overlap.py. the hash is committed.<br/>the PRIMARY family is exactly 3 tests: H1, H2, H3. Holm covers those 3.<br/>MoRF against Random, MoRF against Weight-matched and the<br/>rank correlations SUPPORT the claim. They do not enter the family"]
    subgraph CH["<b>choose_test.py</b> · BUILT · the test must fit the distribution"]
        direction LR
        K1["<b>1 · the design is paired</b><br/>same window, two arms<br/>→ use the differences D_i"]
        K2["<b>2 · find the shape of D</b> · THE RULE<br/>bootstrap the sample SKEWNESS of the non-zero D.<br/>symmetric = the 95 percent skew interval holds 0,<br/>or the absolute skew is below SYMMETRY_SKEW_TOL = 0.5.<br/>also report Shapiro-Wilk, kurtosis and the share positive"]
        K3["<b>3a · symmetric</b><br/>→ Wilcoxon signed-rank, one-sided.<br/>it tests the PSEUDOMEDIAN, the<br/>Hodges-Lehmann location.<br/>that equals the median only<br/>when D is symmetric. say so"]
        K4["<b>3b · skewed or heavy tail</b><br/>→ sign test on the MEDIAN.<br/>the effect is the share of<br/>positive D among the non-zero D.<br/>never a plain t-test"]
        K5["<b>4 · the rows are NOT independent</b><br/>windows overlap · pedestrians repeat · only 5 scenes<br/>→ p from the SIGN-FLIP permutation by <b>COMPONENT</b><br/>→ CI from the PAIRS cluster bootstrap by component"]
        K1 --> K2
        K2 --> K3
        K2 --> K4
        K6["<b>5 · why NOT the other tests</b><br/>paired t-test → D is long-tailed. the mean is not the target<br/>plain bootstrap → it assumes independent rows. they are not<br/>OLS or ANOVA on raw rows → the same independence fault<br/>Bonferroni → Holm dominates it at no cost<br/>chi-square → the outcome is continuous, not a count"]
        K3 --> K5
        K4 --> K5
        K5 --> K6
    end
    YC["<b>data_checks.py</b> · BUILT · check that the input fits the test<br/>every window has the 4 ordered arms at step 1 · print the attrition table<br/>weight_matched matches MASS, not count, so it needs only ONE row.<br/>zero differences: keep them, use the Pratt rule · the small window is dropped"]
    Y1["<b>h1_morf_vs_lerf.py</b> · BUILT<br/>D_i = shift(MoRF) − shift(LeRF)<br/>H0-1: the location of D is 0 or less.<br/>also report MoRF against Random and<br/>MoRF against Weight-matched.<br/>the weight-matched partner comes from<br/>removed_mass, never from n_removed"]
    Y2["<b>h2_beyond_proximity.py</b> · BUILT<br/>D_i = shift(MoRF) − shift(Nearest)<br/>H0-2: removal of high-attention edges does<br/>NOT give a larger forecast shift than<br/>removal of the nearest-neighbour edges.<br/>the ARM comparison is the primary test. every window stays in,<br/>because a tie is real data and the Pratt rule pulls toward the null.<br/>4 supporting rows: the disagreeing windows alone,<br/>Spearman rho( attn , dist ), the partial correlation of attn<br/>with the single-edge shift GIVEN distance, and the attention shuffle"]
    Y3["<b>h3_context.py</b> · BUILT<br/>FI_i = b0 + b·context + <b>scene FIXED effects</b><br/>context = density, n_agents,<br/>closing_speed, inv_ttc<br/>H0-3: every b = 0 AND every scene term = 0.<br/><b>OLS with scene fixed effects. ONE joint p from the</b><br/><b>WILD CLUSTER BOOTSTRAP by component.</b><br/>5 scenes is too few for a random intercept.<br/>check the collinearity first. report partial R2"]
    YV["<b>validate.py</b> · BUILT · check that the answer holds<br/>LOSO per scene · the n_removed sweep 1 to 5 · another module (decoder, cross) ·<br/>another time collapse (max, last) · the second mask policy (weight_zero) ·<br/>the attention shuffle. at n_removed 1 every row is a LOOKUP into the single rows,<br/>so no row costs a forward pass. every row runs through h1_morf_vs_lerf.test_paired,<br/>so one effect definition serves the whole study.<br/>LOSO shows heterogeneity. it is NOT 5 more tests. NO p here enters a family.<br/>If MoRF does not beat Random above the noise floor, the answer is<br/>'attention is NOT faithful'. That is a result, not a failure."]
    YF["<b>figures.py</b> · BUILT · FIVE figures, the house style of eda/plotting.py<br/>1 · curves_figure: mean shift against n_removed per arm, with a bootstrap band<br/>2 · paired_figure: the histogram of D for H1 and H2, the median and the zero line<br/>3 · fi_figure: the faithfulness index per scene<br/>4 · h3_figure: the coefficient plot with the cluster-robust interval<br/>5 · loso_figure: a forest plot of the location per scene.<br/>a band of a figure is a picture, NOT a reported interval"]
    Y0 --> CH
    CH --> YC
    YC --> Y1 & Y2 & Y3
    Y1 & Y2 & Y3 --> YV
    YV --> YF
end
subgraph ST["src/stats/ · effects.py ★ CATHERINE · loso.py ★ GRACE · the other 4 files ★ PREM · EVERY FILE EXISTS"]
    direction TB
    T1["<b>clustered.py</b> · BUILT · the primary unit is the <b>CONNECTED COMPONENT</b><br/>of the pedestrian by time-block graph. config.CLUSTER_UNIT holds it.<br/>the pedestrian and the time block CROSS: 37 percent of pedestrians<br/>span more than 1 block, so neither unit nests inside the other.<br/>a pilot of 2,418 real windows gives the false positive rate against<br/>a target of 0.05: pedestrian 0.085 · time block 0.115 · component 0.030.<br/>the component is the coarsest unit that respects both.<br/>the frozen table gives <b>72 components over 481 windows</b>.<br/>H1 and H2 → resample COMPONENTS with replacement, the pairs bootstrap.<br/>H3 → wild cluster bootstrap on the restricted regression residuals.<br/>they are not the same tool. print n_clusters beside every p"]
    T6["<b>permutation.py</b> · BUILT · where the p-value comes from<br/>PRIMARY: flip the SIGN of D_i inside the COMPONENT.<br/>Pratt ranks keep a zero. exact for a paired design,<br/>and it needs no GPU.<br/>SECONDARY: shuffle the attention weight inside the<br/>scene and re-rank. every new D is a LOOKUP into the<br/>single rows, so this test also costs no forward pass"]
